# Changelog

All notable changes to this guide are documented here.

The format follows [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/).

---

## [1.0.0] - 2026-05-24

### Added

- Initial release of the complete installation guide
- Step-by-step instructions for Fedora 44 KDE Plasma with NVIDIA RTX GPU
- RPM Fusion driver installation via `akmod-nvidia` (595.xx branch)
- NVIDIA Container Toolkit setup with CDI specification generation
- SELinux configuration for GPU container passthrough
- Validated `compose.yml` for Ollama and Open WebUI with Podman Compose
- `docs/troubleshooting.md` covering driver, CDI, SELinux, container, and networking issues
- `docs/advanced-gpu.md` covering layer offloading, VRAM planning, quantisation, and environment tuning
- `CONTRIBUTING.md` with writing style guidelines and commit message format
- GitHub issue templates for bug reports and documentation improvements
- GitHub pull request template
- MIT Licence

### Notes

- NVIDIA has not yet published an official `cuda-fedora44.repo` as of May 2026.
  RPM Fusion is the validated and recommended driver installation method for Fedora 44.
- Validated against Fedora 44 KDE Plasma (released 28 April 2026), Ollama v0.24.0,
  and Podman 5.x.
